      "body": "### ROCm results for this batch (per-test) — why it was closed\n\nSource: `jit-kernel-unit-test-amd-rocm720` run [28770896639](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/28770896639) (MI325 / gfx942, `continue_on_error` so every file ran).\n\n| Test | Result | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_dsv32_indexer_fusion.py` | ✅ pass | Has an `is_hip()` code path; compiles and passes on ROCm |\n| `test_hicache.py` | ❌ fail | CUDA-only kernel: hicache write-back uses CUDA PTX inline asm (`invalid input constraint 'l'`) |\n| `test_awq_dequantize.py` | ❌ fail | CUDA-only (AWQ) — already caught by the `awq` token in `_NVIDIA_ONLY_KERNEL_PATTERNS` |\n| `test_kpool_topk_transform.py` | ❌ fail | CUDA-only kernel: `kpool_topk_transform.cuh` includes `cuda_fp16.h` |\n| `deepseek_v4/test_topk_v2.py` | ❌ fail | CUDA-only kernel: `deepseek_v4/topk_impl.cuh` includes `cooperative_groups.h` |\n| `minimax/test_minimax_qknorm_rope.py` | ❌ fail | CUDA-only kernel: fused gemma-qknorm-rope uses `nv_bfloat16` / CUDA inline asm |\n\n**Outcome:** only `test_dsv32_indexer_fusion` is ROCm-portable; it was **moved into #30212**, and this PR was **closed** (superseded). The 5 CUDA-only kernels are tracked for dashboard exclusion in ROCm/sglang-ci#297.",
